# Build context for docker/allinone/Dockerfile. The context is the repo root, so anything not
# listed here is uploaded to the daemon and may end up in a layer.
#
# Two jobs: keep the image minimal, and make it impossible for a local secret or a host-built
# virtualenv to be copied in. backend/.env holds a real API key; backend/studio/.venv is 131 MB
# of host-architecture wheels that COPY backend/studio would otherwise bake straight into
# /app/studio. No blanket *.log rule here: the 33 golden parser samples under backend/packs are
# .log files and are the evidence the reconstruction proof runs against.

# --- version control and tooling
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.claude
**/.pytest_cache

# --- secrets and local configuration (never in an image we hand to a judge)
.env
**/.env
!**/*.env.example
deploy/secrets/*
!deploy/secrets/*.example
**/.chat_sessions.json
**/.studio_secret

# --- host-built artefacts: rebuilt inside the builder stages, never copied from the host
**/.venv
**/venv
**/node_modules
frontend/dist
bin/
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.test
.gocache

# --- local development state and run logs (explicit paths, never a *.log glob)
.dev-logs
.demo-traffic.log
.defense-traffic.log
.llm-traffic.log
data/
/data

# --- test code that nothing at run time imports
# Only the Python unit tests. backend/packs/tests is NOT excluded and must never be: those 33
# .log files are the golden samples that `aletheia test-pack` reconstructs byte for byte, which
# is the project's central claim and is re-checked inside the shipped image.
backend/studio/tests
backend/studio/requirements-dev.txt
backend/pytest.ini
backend/engine/testdata

# --- not part of the product, or not copied by the Dockerfile
personal
docs
scripts
setup.bat
setup.ps1
*.tar
*.tar.gz
